  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "While Vika accepts an evening invitation from Nikolai over the phone, Nagiyev gathers the cooks in the kitchen so Katya can demonstrate her molecular tomato soup.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, здравствуйте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы уже получили мой презент?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо, но не стоило.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я очень хочу с вами встретиться.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Попытаться вас убедить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Договорились? Ну хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вечером я пришлю за вами машину.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Сейчас Катя продемонстрирует блюда молекулярной кухни.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Это ресторан! Должно быть съедобно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Это томатный суп.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Да, конечно, попробуйте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Рука дрожит.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Алло, здравствуйте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello, good afternoon.' Notice how Russian expresses 'hello' and 'hello' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы уже получили мой презент?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Have you already received my gift?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'you' before landing on 'gift'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо, но не стоило.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you, but you shouldn't have.' The negative particle sits right before the verb meaning 'to cost' to negate the statement.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я очень хочу с вами встретиться.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I really want to meet with you.' The meaning hinges on 'I' working together with 'to meet' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Попытаться вас убедить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'To try to convince you.' Notice the reflexive suffix on the verb meaning 'to try', turning the action back on the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Договорились? Ну хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Agreed? Well, all right.' The meaning hinges on 'agreed' working together with 'well' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вечером я пришлю за вами машину.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In the evening I will send a car for you.' Vika anchors the line on 'in the evening', while 'car' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Сейчас Катя продемонстрирует блюда молекулярной кухни.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now Katya will demonstrate dishes of molecular cuisine.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'now' and finishing on 'kitchen'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Это ресторан! Должно быть съедобно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is a restaurant! It must be edible.' Notice how Russian expresses 'this' and 'edible' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Katya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Это томатный суп.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is tomato soup.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'this' before landing on 'soup'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "katya",
      "t": "Да, конечно, попробуйте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, of course, try it.' Katya brings out the contrast between 'yes' and 'of course' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Рука дрожит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My hand is trembling.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'hand', while 'trembles' completes the thought. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
